# Keeps data/ present in a fresh clone.
#
# The start command passes --localstorage-file=data/..., and node opens that path
# before any application code runs — so the directory has to exist already or the
# process dies at startup. On a host with a mounted volume the mount point covers
# this; on a plain clone (and on the first boot before a volume is attached) this
# file is what makes the path valid.
